From e36a3033e473b19401a110324a0e7079064adcee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/37] clk: qcom: provide bounded TCL display and GPU clock
 trees

The ACPI display/GPU devices need explicit GCC, DISPCC, GPUCC and GDSC
providers in place of OF clock and domain lookup.

Add guarded platform providers, bounded GCC register access and
standalone domain publication. Preserve firmware PLL assumptions where
required and expose consumer clocks through explicitly owned lookup
aliases. Allocate complete clkdev identifiers and verify resolution
during registration so long names cannot silently truncate. Provider
cleanup releases the owned aliases. The board coordinators still assign
consumers and retain power dependencies; this is not a complete
replacement for the SoC DT clock topology.
